---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { societe } from '../../data/legal';
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy policy | Lifitness Dakar"
  description="How Lifitness Dakar handles your data: contact forms, WhatsApp, no server storage, cookies and your rights under Senegalese law."
  path="/en/privacy"
  pageName="Privacy policy"
>
  <h2>1. Principles</h2>
  <p>
    This site is a static showcase website. It contains no database, no user
    account and no advertising tracker. We collect the minimum: only what you
    choose to send us.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data collected via forms</h2>
  <p>
    The site forms (free trial, contact, newsletter) collect: name, phone, email
    (optional), preferred gym, goal and level (trial form), free message.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>This data does not pass through a server we own.</strong>
    On validation, your browser opens WhatsApp with a pre-filled message (or
    your email software for the email copy). The site itself stores nothing: no
    form data is saved on the hosting.
  </p>
  <p>
    The data you then send us (via WhatsApp, email, phone or at the gym) is used
    solely to: answer your request, schedule your trial session, manage your
    membership and send you practical information if you consent.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Legal basis and purpose</h2>
  <p>
    Processing is based on your consent (voluntary sending of a form or message)
    and on the performance of our services (membership management). In
    accordance with Senegalese law No. 2008-12 of January 25, 2008 on the
    protection of personal data, processing related to membership is subject to
    the required formalities with the CDP.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Recipients</h2>
  <p>
    Only the teams of {societe.nomCommercial} (front desk and coaching staff of
    both gyms) access your data, within the limits required for your follow-up.
    No data is sold or transferred to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Retention period</h2>
  <p>
    Member data is kept for the duration of the membership, then archived for
    the period of legal obligations. Simple contact requests not followed by a
    membership are deleted after 12 months.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cookies and audience measurement</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses <strong>no tracking cookies</strong> by default. A
    privacy-friendly audience measurement tool (Plausible or Umami, without
    cookies or individual profiling) may be enabled later; it counts aggregated
    visits without identifying people. This page will be updated if so.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access, rectify, delete and object to your data. To
    exercise them, write to us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${societe.email}`}>{societe.email}</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Phone:{' '}
      <a href={`tel:${societe.telephone.replace(/[^+\d]/g, '')}`}>
        {societe.telephone}
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>Mail: {societe.siege}</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You may also file a complaint with the Senegalese Commission for the
    Protection of Personal Data (CDP).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    WhatsApp and email exchanges travel on third-party infrastructures beyond
    our control. For any sensitive information, prefer an exchange at the gym or
    by phone.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
